  "answer": "Fixed and verified.\n\n**Change (src/ledger.ts only):**\n```diff\n-    sum -= entry.amount\n+    sum += entry.amount\n```\nThe loop was subtracting each entry; it now adds. `Entry` and the `total(entries: Entry[]): number` signature are unchanged, and starting `sum` at `0` still yields `0` for an empty array.\n\n**Test result** (`bun test`):\n```\ntest/oracle.test.ts:\n(pass) totals add [0.14ms]\n 1 pass\n 0 fail\n 3 expect() calls\n```\nAll three assertions pass: `[4, 6] → 10`, `[] → 0`, `[-3] → -3`. Note that a negative `amount` is still added, so `[{amount: -3}]` legitimately returns `-3` — the fix is about the operation, not about rejecting negative entries.\n\nAGENTS.md, package.json, and test/oracle.test.ts were left untouched, and no configuration or runner changes were made."
